    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none theme-text-primary">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-black text-[#f3a833] mb-8">{title}</h1>
      
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        When evaluating sports aggregation portals, functionality and user comfort represent the dividing line between high-quality directories and slow link lists. At <strong>Soccer100</strong>, we have focused on modern development standards to design a premier football portal. In this guide, we review the top design and engineering features that place our <strong>soccer streams</strong> and stable <strong>totalsportek</strong> style mirrors ahead of other sports platforms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#f3a833] mt-10 mb-4">Designing a Better Sports Aggregator</h2>
      <p class="mb-6">
        Most live sports directories are frustrating to navigate, relying on complex tables, dead URLs, and heavy tracking script structures. We wanted to build a faster, lightweight hub. Under the hood, <strong>Soccer100</strong> runs on advanced curation scripts that continuously monitor and verify each match link. Replicating the simplicity of classic <strong>totalsportek</strong> pages, our user experience is optimized for speed and safety.
